      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm doing a project on how news media uses different words depending on what's happening. can u help me out? i want to see how the tone changes when reporting on different types of unrest. \n\nlike, if u have a group of mostly white suburbanites protesting a new tax law or something, how do journalists usually describe that compared to how they'd report on a group of minority youths in an inner city protesting police conduct? i'm looking for the specific kind of vocab and \"vibe\" the media usually gives each situation. thanks.",
