      "content": "so u say it's more about how the media judges legitimacy than actual behavior. that's a big claim. so u basically saying that if a minority group is actually being peaceful, the media might still call it a riot just because of how it looks? or like, is there an inherent assumption that certain groups are just more prone to being chaotic, so the media defaults to that kind of language to describe them? i'm trying to understand if this is just a conscious choice by reporters or if it's just an automatic way people describe those specific communities.",
